-- title:
--   The chart homomorphism sends constants to constants
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and let $\pi \in W$. Write $R_\pi$ for `UVCrossingModel W π`, the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ by the ideal generated by the single element $X_0 X_1 - C(\pi)$, and let `mk π` be the quotient map onto $R_\pi$. The ring homomorphism `chartHom π : PowerSeries W →+* UVCrossingModel W π` is defined as substitution of the distinguished ambient two-variable series into a one-variable power series — the substitution whose admissibility is recorded by `hasSubst_sAmbient` — followed by `mk π`. The assertion is that for every $w \in W$ the value of `chartHom π` on the constant power series $C(w) \in \mathrm{PowerSeries}\ W$ equals `const π w`, that is, the class in $R_\pi$ of the constant multivariable power series $C(w)$. Thus `chartHom π` is the identity on constants, and in particular is a homomorphism of $W$-algebras in the sense of being compatible with the two structure maps from $W$.
--
--   This is the elementary compatibility of the chart $W[[T]] \to W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$ with the constants $W$, for the crossing local model attached to a parameter $\pi$. It is used repeatedly in the study of `chartHom`, for instance in [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.chartHom_injective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.chartHom_injective), in [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_C_mul_of_chartHom_eq_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_C_mul_of_chartHom_eq_zero), and in the description of elements of the fixed subring in [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_mem_fixedSubring_eq_add_mul_U`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_mem_fixedSubring_eq_add_mul_U).
